6 lost 16.4 points and the lead fell from +20.8 to +4.4. The engine's choice was E8. Black had a winning position and let it go in one move."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "H4 lost 11.5 points and turned a +6.5 lead into -5.1. Opus 5.5 pushed along the right side, where White's stones at H5 and H6 were already in place, and the lead did not return."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "A5 on the left edge lost 9.3 points and dropped Black from -6.2 to -15.5. White's A7 next lost 9.6 points and put the game back to about -6, where it stayed until the two passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and report group liberties (with a danger flag) and a simple area score with optional dead stones removed; neither generates, scores or ranks candidate moves nor looks ahead, so they only inspect the current position.", "stop": false}}